# VariableExport Project Rules

You are an expert frontend architect working on a clean, scalable, shadcn/ui-style architecture inside a Vite + React + TypeScript project.

## 🏗 TECH STACK (MANDATORY)

### Use:
- Vite (React + TS template)
- React 18+
- TypeScript
- TailwindCSS
- shadcn/ui (installed via CLI)
- class-variance-authority (cva)
- lucide-react
- tailwind-merge
- clsx

### DO NOT use:
- styled-components
- CSS modules
- inline styles
- Chakra UI
- MUI
- Ant Design

**Only Tailwind + shadcn/ui.**

## 📁 PROJECT STRUCTURE (MUST FOLLOW EXACTLY)

```
/src
  /components
    /ui              → shadcn components ONLY
    /system          → token-driven abstractions
    /layout          → containers, wrappers
  /lib
    utils.ts         → cn() + helper utilities
    tokens.ts        → design tokens (parsed later)
  /hooks
  /pages or /screens
  /styles
    globals.css
    tailwind.css
  /config
    theme-config.ts  → light/dark theme mapping
```

**RULES:**
- ❗ Never place UI code in pages or screens.
- ❗ Only use /components/ui for true UI primitives.

## 🎨 SHADCN/UI RULESET

ALL UI components MUST follow these core rules:

### ✔ Use cva() for styling variants:
```typescript
import { cva, type VariantProps } from "class-variance-authority";
```

### ✔ Use cn() for merging classes:
```typescript
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"
```

### ✔ All components MUST be defined like this:

```typescript
const Button = React.forwardRef<..., ButtonProps>(
  ({ className, variant, size, ...props }, ref) => {
    return (
      <button
        ref={ref}
        className={cn(buttonVariants({ variant, size }), className)}
        {...props}
      />
    );
  }
);
Button.displayName = "Button";
export { Button, buttonVariants };
```

**RULES:**
- ❗ NEVER use inline style={{}} unless dynamic or calculated.
- ❗ NEVER write custom CSS — only Tailwind classes.
- ❗ NEVER put logic inside UI components.

## 🧩 COMPONENT NAMING RULES

Every component must match this pattern:

- Button → /components/ui/button.tsx
- Card → /components/ui/card.tsx
- Input → /components/ui/input.tsx
- Badge → /components/ui/badge.tsx

**RULES:**
- ❗ No capital-letter folders
- ❗ No nested UI inside pages
- ❗ No mixing logic and UI

## 🎛 TOKEN + THEME READY RULESET

This project MUST be ready for token-based theming.

**Files:**
- /lib/tokens.ts → this file will later import parsed tokens
- /config/theme-config.ts → map tokens → Tailwind semantic classes

**RULES:**
Color tokens must map to Tailwind CSS variables:

```css
:root {
  --background: <token>;
  --foreground: <token>;
  --primary: <token>;
  --primary-foreground: <token>;
  ...
}

.dark {
  --background: <token-dark>;
  --foreground: <token-dark>;
  ...
}
```

## 📦 TAILWIND CONFIG RULES

Tailwind MUST be configured as follows:

```javascript
theme.extend = {
  colors: {
    background: "hsl(var(--background))",
    foreground: "hsl(var(--foreground))",
    primary: "hsl(var(--primary))",
    ...
  },
  borderRadius: {
    sm: "var(--radius-sm)",
    md: "var(--radius-md)",
    lg: "var(--radius-lg)"
  },
  spacing: {
    xs: "var(--space-xs)",
    sm: "var(--space-sm)",
    md: "var(--space-md)",
    lg: "var(--space-lg)",
    xl: "var(--space-xl)"
  }
}
```

**RULES:**
- ❗ NEVER hardcode colors or spacing in Tailwind.
- ❗ ALWAYS pull from design tokens.

## 📚 LAYOUT SYSTEM RULES

System-level components:

- /components/layout/Container.tsx → Enforce max-width, padding from tokens
- /components/layout/Section.tsx → For vertical stacking & spacing
- /components/system/TokenTable.tsx → Render tokens visually
- /components/system/ColorSwatch.tsx → Display color tokens in DS

**RULES:**
These components MUST NOT depend on business logic.

## 🧱 SAFE-GUARDS (VERY IMPORTANT)

### ❗ DO NOT:
- Invent new folder structures
- Mix styling systems
- Hardcode colors, spacing, radius, shadows
- Insert unnecessary wrappers
- Generate ugly nested divs

### ❗ ALWAYS:
- Keep code minimal
- Keep UI atomic
- Keep everything reusable
- Use shadcn/ui best practices
- Use cva for variants
- Use cn for merging classes
- Use path alias @ for imports (e.g., @/lib/utils)

## 🔧 PATH ALIASES

Always use path aliases:
- `@/components/*` instead of `../../components/*`
- `@/lib/*` instead of `../../lib/*`
- `@/config/*` instead of `../../config/*`

## 📝 CODE STYLE

- Use TypeScript strictly
- Use React.forwardRef for all components
- Always set displayName for components
- Export both component and variants (e.g., `export { Button, buttonVariants }`)
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Follow accessibility best practices

## 🎯 PRIORITY ORDER

1. Follow project structure EXACTLY
2. Use only Tailwind + shadcn/ui patterns
3. Never hardcode design values
4. Keep components atomic and reusable
5. Use tokens/CSS variables for all design values

